@node Implementing Properties
@subsection Implementing Properties

Properties are provided by resource type implementations through the
following GOOPS methods. A resource type @emph{must} implement all of
these. It's advised to not use these methods directly for modifying
the property set, but instead use the procedures defined above
(@pxref{Accessing Properties}).

Live properties are implemented through a getter, setter, and
remover procedure. These procedures @emph{should} be GOOPS
methods, to allow further specialization by sub-classes. And the
implementing methods (getter, setter, and remover) @emph{should} be
exported from the defining module.

The getter @emph{must} always return a valid propstat object,
containing the corresponding xml tag. However, it may return a 404
propstat (or any other appropriate error code).

Setters and removers should run any pre-conditions for executing their
action, and must return a thunk, which when invoked performs the
action. If a pre-condition failed, then an error must be thrown.
When the property is protected, explicitly @code{protected-property}
must be thrown. If either of remove or set is allowed, then both
@emph{should} be allowed.

@b{TODO} this interface should be changed to a direct system, but with
explicit transactions with commits and rollbacks. The current API
will, for example fail when setting extended file attributes, since a
